		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=43752#p43752"><![CDATA[
Hard to say from just the video, so this probably won't be accurate, but maybe it'll still help in a rubber-ducking kind of way.<br><br>The first thing it makes me think is that somewhere in your velocity/restitution code you're using full Δt instead of the substep Δt. You could try turning off restitution to see if you can make more stable stacks (that will have bounce out problems when contact ends, but at least shouldn't explode). If that works, that's a very good sign the restitution is somehow messed up, whether a Δt problem or something else.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=14001">jak</a> — Tue Dec 07, 2021 10:30 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
